// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Staff360 — Firestore rules SNIPPET (do NOT deploy this file on its own:
// it would replace every existing HisaabNow rule).
//
// Paste these match blocks INSIDE your existing
//   service cloud.firestore { match /databases/{database}/documents { … } }
// in C:\dev\hisaabnow\firestore.rules, then deploy to STAGING first:
//   firebase deploy --only firestore:rules --project hisaabnow-staging
//
// Design: every Staff360 collection is server-owned. All reads and writes go
// through the staff360* callable functions, which check sign-in, shop
// membership, role and plan with the Admin SDK. Clients get NO direct access,
// so editing localStorage / URL / client state cannot grant a plan, read
// another shop, or forge a punch.
//
// These paths are deliberately top-level (not under /shops/{shopId}) so an
// existing recursive rule like  match /shops/{shopId}/{doc=**}  cannot
// accidentally open them up (Firestore ORs every matching allow).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    match /staff360/{shopId}/{document=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
    match /staff360Entitlements/{shopId} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
    match /staff360Config/{docId} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
    match /staff360WaSchedule/{shopId} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }

// CHECK BEFORE DEPLOYING: if your existing rules contain a catch-all such as
//   match /{document=**} { allow read, write: if request.auth != null; }
// the denies above are overridden (rules are OR'd). Remove or narrow that
// catch-all first — otherwise plan entitlements are client-writable.
